---
description: Autosave, atomic writes, snapshots, and storage rules; protects the user's writing from loss
globs: src-tauri/**,src/lib/storage/**,src/lib/save/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Autosave a few seconds after the last change (debounced) and on window close/blur; show a subtle saved/saving indicator.
- Writes must be crash-safe: SQLite transactions (WAL mode) or write temp file then atomic rename. Never write in place.
- Store chapter content as TipTap/ProseMirror JSON plus a derived plain-text copy for search/word count. Include a schema version and migrations.
- Local snapshots: rolling (e.g. hourly + daily), restorable from the UI. Restore must be tested.
- The live project file stays on local disk. Backups are snapshot files written to a user-chosen folder (e.g. inside Google Drive for desktop), never the live database.
- All persistence goes through a storage interface (`save`, `load`, `listSnapshots`, `restore`) so a Drive API backend can be added later.
- Surface save failures clearly and keep the unsaved text in memory; never swallow errors.
- Never delete user data without a confirmation and a recoverable snapshot.
